<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:architecture-evolves-semantics-first> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "architecture-evolves-semantics-first" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:architecture-evolves-semantics-first> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "Architecture changes by changing the model first, then the required verifications, then enforcement, then implementation, and finally by new evidence and proof." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:architecture-evolves-semantics-first> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "An implementation change that violates a declared rule is a violation, never a redefinition of the intended architecture." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:architecture-evolves-semantics-first> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:evidence-must-be-attributable> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "evidence-must-be-attributable" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:evidence-must-be-attributable> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "A passing tool invocation is proof only when its evidence carries the requirement identity, the source revision, the verification mechanism, the tool and version, the effective configuration digest, the invocation, the result and its own evidence digest." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:evidence-must-be-attributable> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The existence of a configuration file is not proof that continuous integration executed it, and a green tool run with no link to a requirement proves nothing about that requirement." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:evidence-must-be-attributable> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:mandatory-failure-blocks-realisation> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "mandatory-failure-blocks-realisation" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:mandatory-failure-blocks-realisation> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "A build is not realised merely because it compiles and its tests pass. If a requirement the model marks mandatory fails its verification, that requirement is unsatisfied and realisation fails." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:mandatory-failure-blocks-realisation> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A mandatory requirement may not carry advisory severity. Recording a violation as informational to obtain a green build is a defect in the assurance model, not a dispensation." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:mandatory-failure-blocks-realisation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:requirement-must-project-to-work> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "requirement-must-project-to-work" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:requirement-must-project-to-work> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "A mandatory requirement is complete only when an unbroken attributable path exists from the model assertion through a recognised obligation, a contract, derived work, a realised artifact, a validation, evidence and proof, to a conformance state." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:requirement-must-project-to-work> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A requirement that generates no work while unsatisfied is a projection defect, and a validation result that cannot be traced to the requirement it verifies is an assurance defect. Existing in the graph is not completion." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:requirement-must-project-to-work> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:tools-are-not-requirements> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "tools-are-not-requirements" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:tools-are-not-requirements> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "A requirement states the property that must hold, independently of whichever mechanism proves it. A named tool enters the model only where use of that exact tool is itself normative." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:tools-are-not-requirements> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Today's tooling choice must never define tomorrow's semantic model." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:tools-are-not-requirements> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:verification-must-be-verified> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "verification-must-be-verified" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:verification-must-be-verified> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "For every boundary the model marks mandatory, a planted representative violation must be shown to fail its verification, and then be removed." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:verification-must-be-verified> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Without this, permanently green output is indistinguishable from a verification that observes nothing." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:verification-must-be-verified> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:IntegrityInvariant> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
