<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:invariantProtected> <urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:requirement-must-project-to-work> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:invariantProtected> <urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:tools-are-not-requirements> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:invariantProtected> <urn:usf:architecture-assurance-invariant:verification-must-be-verified> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Only two assurance axes are new: severity and verification class. Everything else an architectural fitness function needs is already carried by DeliveryFacet, which states the invariant, its applicability, its admissible evidence class and its requirement class." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Reuse is deliberate and load-bearing. Requirement, SemanticContract, DeliveryContract, DeliveryFacet, Evidence, EvidenceRequirement, ProofObligation, ProofAlgorithm, ProofResult, RealisationPermission, ValidationEvidenceModel, IntegrityInvariant, WorkPacket, invariant, declaresPort, fulfilsPort, servedByAdapter, verificationMethod, dependsOn and the eight Environment resources already exist and are not restated." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This extension adds no lifecycle. MODEL, EVIDENCE, PROOF, CONTRACT, REALISATION and VALIDATION are the existing urn:usf:stage resources, and architecture is a dimension travelling through them rather than a parallel layer." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-assurance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Generic vocabulary for stating an architecture as verifiable semantics and for carrying architecture, build and assurance requirements through the Semantic Build lifecycle USF already owns. Product-neutral, and naming no tool." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-assurance> .
